The dark-mode flicker script reads `localStorage.getItem('object-ui-theme')`, but the actual ThemeProvider persistence keys are `${storageKey}-name` and `${storageKey}-mode` with default `storageKey = 'objectui-theme'` (so `objectui-theme-name` / `objectui-theme-mode`). This example won’t reflect real persisted settings unless it uses the same keys and mode semantics.
```suggestion
  const storageKey = 'objectui-theme';
  const modeKey = storageKey + '-mode';
  const themeMode = localStorage.getItem(modeKey) || 'system';
  const isDark =
    themeMode === 'dark' ||
    (themeMode === 'system' && matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)').matches);
