```

The `I18nProvider` example uses props `locale` and `messages`, but `@object-ui/i18n`’s `I18nProvider` takes `config`, `instance`, and optional `loadLanguage` (see `packages/i18n/src/provider.tsx`). As written, this snippet won’t compile for users following the guide.
```suggestion
const i18n = /* your i18n instance */;

const i18nConfig = {
  defaultLocale: 'en',
};

<I18nProvider config={i18nConfig} instance={i18n}>
```

The “Register Components” snippet references `registerAllComponents` and passes `Registry` into both registration functions, but `@object-ui/components` exports `initializeComponents()` (registration happens via side effects) and `@object-ui/fields` exports `registerAllFields()` with no parameters. As written, this setup code won’t compile/work for consumers.
```suggestion
import { initializeComponents } from '@object-ui/components';
import { registerAllFields } from '@object-ui/fields';

initializeComponents();
registerAllFields();
```

The peer dependency check only verifies `react` for `@object-ui/react`, but both `@object-ui/react` and `@object-ui/components` list `react-dom` as a peer dependency too. As written, `objectui doctor` can report a “healthy” setup even when `react-dom` is missing. Consider checking for both `react` and `react-dom` (and possibly their versions) when ObjectUI packages are present.
```suggestion
      }
      if (allDeps['@object-ui/react'] && !allDeps['react-dom']) {
        console.log(chalk.yellow('⚠️ @object-ui/react requires react-dom as a peer dependency'));
        issues++;
      }
      if (allDeps['@object-ui/components'] && !allDeps['tailwindcss']) {
        console.log(chalk.yellow('⚠️ @object-ui/components requires tailwindcss as a peer dependency'));
        issues++;
      }
      if (allDeps['@object-ui/components'] && !allDeps['react']) {
        console.log(chalk.yellow('⚠️ @object-ui/components requires react as a peer dependency'));
        issues++;
      }
      if (allDeps['@object-ui/components'] && !allDeps['react-dom']) {
        console.log(chalk.yellow('⚠️ @object-ui/components requires react-dom as a peer dependency'));
        issues++;
      }
```

The new schema examples don’t match the actual `@object-ui/types` schema shapes:
- `form` doesn’t define an `actions: [{ type: 'submit', ... }]` node type (FormSchema uses `submitLabel`/`cancelLabel` or `actions` as SchemaNode[]).
- `dashboard` widgets in types require `{ id, component, layout }`, not `{ type: 'stat-card', ... }`.
These examples should be updated to valid schemas so users can copy/paste them successfully.
